nodejs22 provides Node.js 22.23.5 as a standalone host tool.

Installed location
  Linux/macOS: tools/nodejs22/bin/node, npm, npx
  Windows:     tools/nodejs22/node.exe, npm.cmd, npx.cmd

Add the appropriate directory to PATH to use node/npm/npx:
  Linux/macOS: <vcpkg-root>/installed/<triplet>/tools/nodejs22/bin
  Windows:     <vcpkg-root>\installed\<triplet>\tools\nodejs22

Node 22 runs on macOS 11.0+; the builtin vcpkg-tool-nodejs (Node 24) is built
for macOS 13.5+ and fails on older systems with a dyld libc++ error.

This port installs a prebuilt binary for the target OS and architecture.
Same OS/architecture with a different linkage triplet (for example
x64-osx-dynamic) is supported; a real host/target mismatch prints a warning.
